[31m-      <h2>LLM Pipeline — Gemma-3 + LangChain</h2>[m
[31m-    </div>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-    <p>The LLM is what turns a detection event into a human-readable maintenance report entry. Here's exactly how to set it up and use it.</p>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-    <h3>Setting up Ollama + Gemma-3</h3>[m
[31m-    <div class="codeblock">[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># Step 1: Install Ollama on your laptop</span>[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># Go to ollama.com, download and install for your OS</span>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># Step 2: Pull the Gemma-3 model (do this BEFORE the hackathon — it's 8GB)</span>[m
[31m-ollama pull gemma3:12b[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># Step 3: Run Ollama (it starts a local server at localhost:11434)</span>[m
[31m-ollama serve[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># Step 4: Test it works</span>[m
[31m-curl http://localhost:11434/api/generate -d '{[m
[31m-  "model": "gemma3:12b",[m
[31m-  "prompt": "Say hello",[m
[31m-  "stream": false[m
[31m-}'[m
[31m-    </div>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-    <h3>The LangChain prompt that generates the report</h3>[m
[31m-    <div class="codeblock">[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># backend/llm_worker.py</span>[m
[31m-<span class="ck">from</span> langchain_community.llms <span class="ck">import</span> Ollama[m
[31m-<span class="ck">from</span> langchain_core.output_parsers <span class="ck">import</span> JsonOutputParser[m
[31m-<span class="ck">from</span> langchain_core.prompts <span class="ck">import</span> PromptTemplate[m
[31m-<span class="ck">from</span> pydantic <span class="ck">import</span> BaseModel[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># Define the exact structure you want from the LLM</span>[m
[31m-<span class="ck">class</span> <span class="cf">DefectReport</span>(BaseModel):[m
[31m-    severity_level: str        <span class="cc"># "L1", "L2", or "L3"</span>[m
[31m-    severity_label: str        <span class="cc"># "Minor", "Moderate", "Critical"</span>[m
[31m-    recommended_action: str    <span class="cc"># what to do</span>[m
[31m-    urgency_days: int          <span class="cc"># how many days before action needed</span>[m
[31m-    description: str           <span class="cc"># 2-sentence plain English summary</span>[m
[31m-    estimated_cost_inr: str    <span class="cc"># e.g. "₹50,000 – ₹1,20,000"</span>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cv">llm</span> = <span class="cf">Ollama</span>(model=<span class="cs">"gemma3:12b"</span>, base_url=<span class="cs">"http://localhost:11434"</span>)[m
[31m-<span class="cv">parser</span> = <span class="cf">JsonOutputParser</span>(pydantic_object=DefectReport)[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cv">prompt</span> = <span class="cf">PromptTemplate</span>([m
[31m-    template=<span class="cs">"""[m
[31m-You are a structural engineering assistant for Indian infrastructure inspection.[m
[31m-A drone has detected the following defect:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Defect type: {defect_class}[m
[31m-Confidence: {confidence}%[m
[31m-Measured area: {area_cm2} cm²[m
[31m-GPS location: {lat}, {lon}[m
[31m-Structure type: Bridge / Public Building[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Based on IRC 22-2015 standards, provide a structured assessment.[m
[31m-Respond ONLY with a valid JSON object matching this schema:[m
[31m-{format_instructions}[m
[31m-"""</span>,[m
[31m-    input_variables=[<span class="cs">"defect_class"</span>, <span class="cs">"confidence"</span>, <span class="cs">"area_cm2"</span>, <span class="cs">"lat"</span>, <span class="cs">"lon"</span>],[m
[31m-    partial_variables={<span class="cs">"format_instructions"</span>: parser.<span class="cf">get_format_instructions</span>()}[m
[31m-)[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cv">chain</span> = prompt | llm | parser[m
[31m-[m
[31m-<span class="cc"># Call this function for each detection</span>[m
[31m-<span class="ck">async def</span> <span class="cf">generate_report_entry</span>(detection: dict) -> DefectReport:[m
[31m-    <span class="ck">return await</span> chain.<span class="cf">ainvoke</span>({[m
[31m-        <span class="cs">"defect_class"</span>: detection[<span class="cs">"class"</span>],[m
[31m-        <span class="cs">"confidence"</span>: <span class="cf">round</span>(detection[<span class="cs">"conf"</span>] * <span class="cn">100</span>, <span class="cn">1</span>),[m
[31m-        <span class="cs">"area_cm2"</span>: detection[<span class="cs">"area_cm2"</span>],[m
[31m-        <span class="cs">"lat"</span>: detection[<span class="cs">"gps"</span>][<span class="cs">"lat"</span>],[m
[31m-        <span class="cs">"lon"</span>: detection[<span class="cs">"gps"</span>][<span class="cs">"lon"</span>][m
[31m-    })[m
[31m-    </div>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-    <div class="callout callout-purple">[m
[31m-      <div class="callout-label">Key insight</div>[m
[31m-      <p>The <code>JsonOutputParser</code> with a Pydantic model tells LangChain to validate that Gemma-3's output matches the schema. If the LLM returns badly formatted JSON, LangChain throws an error you can catch. Always wrap LLM calls in try/except during the hackathon — LLMs occasionally output garbage.</p>[m
[31m-    </div>[m
