[31m-  <div class="sec">[m
[31m-    <div class="sec-header">[m
[31m-      <span class="sec-num">01</span>[m
[31m-      <h2>The Problem — India's Infrastructure Crisis</h2>[m
[31m-      <div class="sec-line"></div>[m
[31m-    </div>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-    <div class="big-quote">[m
[31m-      "India has over 1.5 lakh bridges, thousands of government buildings, hundreds of dams, and crores of square feet of industrial infrastructure — and almost none of it is inspected with any form of intelligence or regularity."[m
[31m-      <span>Ground reality, 2024</span>[m
[31m-    </div>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-    <div class="g2">[m
[31m-      <div>[m
[31m-        <p>India is in the middle of the <strong>largest infrastructure buildout in its history</strong>. The government allocated ₹11.11 lakh crore for infrastructure in the 2024–25 budget — roads, bridges, railways, smart cities, hospitals, airports. But here is the problem nobody talks about: <strong>we build fast, but we inspect slow — or not at all.</strong></p>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-        <p>India's National Highway bridges average <strong>over 30 years of age</strong>. Majerhat bridge in Kolkata collapsed in 2018. The Savitri bridge in Raigad killed 28 in 2016. The Morbi bridge in Gujarat killed 135 in 2022. In every case, the same conclusion in the inquiry: <em>no proper inspection had been done in years.</em></p>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-        <p>This is not a budget problem. India spends billions on infrastructure. This is a <strong>methodology problem</strong> — the inspection process is archaic, manual, dangerous, and completely unscalable.</p>[m
[31m-      </div>[m
[31m-      <div>[m
[31m-        <div class="card card-red">[m
[31m-          <h3>How inspections happen today in India</h3>[m
[31m-          <div style="margin-top: 4px;">[m
[31m-            <div style="padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 300;">[m
[31m-              <strong style="color: var(--text-bright);">Manual rope access</strong><br>[m
[31m-              Workers lowered by ropes to inspect bridge undersides. Dangerous, expensive (₹5–15L per audit), covers only accessible sections.[m
[31m-            </div>[m
[31m-            <div style="padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 300;">[m
[31m-              <strong style="color: var(--text-bright);">Visual inspection by juniors</strong><br>[m
[31m-              PWD engineers walk the surface, tap with hammers, write notes. No quantification. Highly subjective. No GPS tagging.[m
[31m-            </div>[m
[31m-            <div style="padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 300;">[m
[31m-              <strong style="color: var(--text-bright);">Inspection frequency</strong><br>[m
[31m-              IRC standards say every 5 years. Reality: most bridges go 10–20 years without a structural audit.[m
[31m-            </div>[m
[31m-            <div style="padding: 10px 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 300;">[m
[31m-              <strong style="color: var(--text-bright);">No digital record</strong><br>[m
[31m-              Findings written in paper registers. No searchable database. No way to track deterioration over time.[m
[31m-            </div>[m
[31m-          </div>[m
[31m-        </div>[m
[31m-      </div>[m
[31m-    </div>[m
[31m-[m
[31m-    <div class="g3" style="margin-top: 8px;">[m
[31m-      <div class="card card-saffron">[m
[31m-        <h3>Scale of the problem</h3>[m
[31m-        <h4>1.5 Lakh Bridges</h4>[m
[31m-        <p style="font-size: 13px;">Across National and State Highways. Average age over 30 years. IRC mandates 5-year inspection cycles that are rarely followed.</p>[m
[31m-      </div>[m
[31m-      <div class="card card-saffron">[m
[31m-        <h3>Worker safety</h3>[m
[31m-        <h4>High-risk jobs</h4>[m
[31m-        <p style="font-size: 13px;">Rope access inspection workers in India earn ₹800–1200/day with no insurance, no safety standards enforcement, and serious fall risk on every job.</p>[m
[31m-      </div>[m
[31m-      <div class="card card-saffron">[m
[31m-        <h3>Beyond bridges</h3>[m
[31m-        <h4>The full scope</h4>[m
[31m-        <p style="font-size: 13px;">The same problem applies to: ISRO launch facilities, nuclear plant exteriors, thermal power plant cooling towers, hospital structural audits, smart city infrastructure, port cranes, and dam faces.</p>[m
[31m-      </div>[m
[31m-    </div>[m
[31m-  </div>[m
